                    "text": "## Stuck after 1 attempt\n\n**Red check:** the preflight, `pnpm test`. `kit/test/no-literals.test.mjs › finds none outside provenance lines` flags `lib/config.mjs:141: home: httpsUrl.default('https://vertuo-omni-loop-galaxy.vercel.app'),`. The other 3268 tests pass.\n**Tried:** 1. I built the slice as planned and ran the full preflight. I made no further attempt, because every fix is outside s1's territory. Hiding the literal from the scanner (splitting the string, or moving it to a file the scanner skips) would only game the guard, so I did not do that either.\n**I believe:** the spec (AC 1, AC 7) puts the arcade's address in `kit/lib/config.mjs` as `signature.home`'s default. It plans the game-words exemption, but not this second guard: `kit/test/no-literals.test.mjs` refuses `/vertuo/i` anywhere in `kit/lib`. The address is a config default a repository can override, not a repository literal, so the narrowest fix is to let that exact host through in `lib/config.mjs` only. It would match the whole host, the way `kit/test/no-game-words.test.mjs` now does, and come with fixture cases showing that \"vertuo\" elsewhere on the line, or in another file, still fails.\n**A person should look at:** `kit/test/no-literals.test.mjs`, because it is outside s1's territory and this slice was told not to change it. Either the wave makes that one exemption, recording it as a decision, or s1's territory gains the file.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
